{
  "$meta": {
    "description": "Clinical overlay layers for the ME/CFS & Fibromyalgia feature set. Every FMA id is a real Foundational Model of Anatomy concept (validated against the FMA ontology shipped with BodyParts3D by `pipeline/run_pipeline.py validate`). Mesh anchors reference BodyParts3D parts in public/models/manifest.json; 'frac' positions [x,y,z] in [0,1] are evaluated against that part's real bounding box in BP3D millimetre space (right = -X, anterior = -Y, superior = +Z), optionally linearly blended between two meshes with 't'.",
    "coordinateSpace": "BodyParts3D 3.0 mm (root: X left-to-right with +X = LEFT, +Y = POSTERIOR, +Z = SUPERIOR; converted to glTF m/Y-up by BP3D_ROOT)",
    "tenderPointSource": "ACR 1990 Fibromyalgia classification criteria (Wolfe et al., Arthritis Rheum 1990;33:160-72): 9 bilateral pairs.",
    "autonomicNote": "BodyParts3D 3.0 ships no vagus-nerve mesh, so the autonomic layer is a schematic: nerve paths are drawn through anchors computed from real loaded organ meshes, and every depicted structure keeps its real FMA concept id. It visualizes the vagal/baroreflex circuitry implicated in dysautonomia (POTS/orthostatic intolerance) in ME/CFS."
  },
